  "methodology_intro": "The assessment aimed to identify, validate and evaluate Internet-exposed vulnerabilities using a combination of automated scanning and manual analysis, adapted to the services identified.\n\nResults were classified by potential impact and ease of exploitation to support remediation prioritization.",
  "conclusion_intro": "The most important finding is the direct Internet exposure of administrative services and of an end-of-support software component.\n\nShould these systems be compromised, there is a risk of unauthorized data access and of pivoting toward the internal networks.\n\nAlthough no active exploitation was performed, the exposed attack surface exceeds the level recommended by security good practices.",
  "conclusion_narrative": "The external-perimeter assessment of Aurora Utilities Ltd. identified an overall high risk level, driven by the exposure of administrative services and an unsupported software component.\n\nSix security findings were identified (1 critical, 2 high, 1 moderate, 1 low and 1 informational). Most can be remediated at the perimeter without application changes.",
  "remediation_directions": [
    {
      "direction": "Remove public access to the administration console",
      "intervention": "Perimeter configuration",
      "urgency": "Immediate"
    },
    {
      "direction": "Restrict RDP to VPN + MFA only",
      "intervention": "Configuration + access process",
      "urgency": "High"
    },
    {
      "direction": "Migrate the end-of-support software component",
      "intervention": "Project, with testing",
      "urgency": "Planned"
    },
    {
      "direction": "Verification scan after remediation",
      "intervention": "Re-assessment",
      "urgency": "After remediation"
    }
  ],
  "test_period": "9 September 2026, 09:00 – 12 September 2026, 17:00 EEST",
  "classification": "Confidential — limited distribution",
  "executive_summary": "The external-perimeter vulnerability assessment of Aurora Utilities Ltd. covered five public IP addresses and their exposed services. Significant exposures were identified, including administrative services reachable directly from the Internet and unsupported software components. The overall risk level is high and requires priority remediation at the perimeter.",
  "assessment_overview": "The objective was to identify and classify Internet-accessible vulnerabilities and exposures on the organization's external perimeter, together with a prioritized remediation plan.",
  "assessment_details": "Grey Box assessment, with limited information provided by the client (IP list and service description). Testing covered service discovery, fingerprinting and vulnerability scanning, without active exploitation.",
